Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: radxa-zero-3: use the RK3566 SoC dtsi

The Radxa ZERO 3E/3W ship with RK3566T SoCs, according to the efuse.
However, Radxa specifies them as RK3566, and its current 6.1 and 6.12
vendor kernels apply the RK3566 OPPs to them. Only an older 5.10 vendor
kernel branch read the efuse and removed the OPPs above 1416 MHz.
Use the RK3566 SoC dtsi, to enable the 1608 MHz and 1800 MHz CPU OPPs
and the 800 MHz GPU OPP. Benchmarks at both CPU OPPs showed no issues.

Link: https://github.com/MichaIng/DietPi/issues/8083
Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/linux-rockchip/2024-October/051988.html
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3.dtsi
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/soc/rockchip,vop2.h>
-#include "rk3566t.dtsi"
+#include "rk3566.dtsi"
 
